	<extensions>
		<genie version="1.0" app="GeNIe 2.0.5494.1" name="Network1" faultnameformat="nodestate">
			<node id="MaximumBankErosion">
				<name>MaximumBankErosion</name>
				<interior color="e5f6f7" />
				<outline color="000080" />
				<font color="000000" name="Arial" size="8" />
				<position>368 57 446 109</position>
				<comment>Assumptions:\nFill terrace = more erosion - most important by several orders of magnitude\nRoad crossings potentially worse than feral pigs - though some interaction\nNo road crossings without fill terraces\nDisturbance second then susceptibility (USGS map between drainage area and stream gradient). \n</comment>
				<barchart active="true" width="128" height="108" />
			</node>
			<node id="DisturbanceType">
				<name>DisturbanceType</name>
				<interior color="e5f6f7" />
				<outline color="000080" />
				<font color="000000" name="Arial" size="8" />
				<position>143 211 227 263</position>
				<barchart active="true" width="229" height="100" />
			</node>
			<node id="FillTerrace">
				<name>FillTerrace</name>
				<interior color="e5f6f7" />
				<outline color="000080" />
				<font color="000000" name="Arial" size="8" />
				<position>410 204 491 244</position>
				<comment>For now we use the proximity to agricultural land as the data source for this node. This data only exists for a single watershed for now, but will eventually exist for all five watersheds. 80% fill terrace, 20% not fill terrace along ag fields\n\nData Source: Proximity to agricultural land from 1950s era agricultur survey.\n</comment>
				<barchart active="true" width="225" height="64" />
			</node>
			<node id="Susceptibility">
				<name>Susceptibility</name>
				<interior color="e5f6f7" />
				<outline color="000080" />
				<font color="000000" name="Arial" size="8" />
				<position>699 201 780 241</position>
				<comment>Data Source: Modeled data layer from John and Corrina. Values range from 0 - 1.\n\n0 when the rainfall is &lt; 10mm/hr. Use the mapped data when the rainfall is &gt;10mm/hr.</comment>
				<barchart active="true" width="128" height="72" />
			</node>
		</genie>
	</extensions>
</smile>
